    "result_text": "Done. The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 2/2 tests, including the new `coreRejectsDuplicateTelephone` and `functionalityAllowsDistinctTelephone`).\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe rule: reject creating an owner whose **normalized** telephone (digits only) already belongs to another owner \u2192 respond **409 Conflict**.\n\nTo keep structural impact low, I added the behaviour as a small, cohesive unit rather than growing any existing method or large class:\n\n1. **New file \u2014 `service/OwnerTelephonePolicy.java`** \u2014 a tiny, self-contained helper with a static `rejectDuplicateTelephone(...)` that normalizes (`\\D` stripped), scans existing owners, and throws a nested `DuplicateTelephoneException` (annotated `@ResponseStatus(CONFLICT)`). No state, no injection, so it adds no complexity to any surrounding class.\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 one added call line before `saveOwner`, plus one import. Because the helper is static, I avoided touching the constructor/fields, keeping this edit to a single line in the large controller class.\n\n3. **`ExceptionControllerAdvice`** \u2014 one small `@ExceptionHandler` that maps the exception to 409 (reusing the existing `detailBuild` helper). This handler is necessary because the advice's catch-all `@ExceptionHandler(Exception.class)` would otherwise turn the exception into a 500.\n\nThree files touched, each changed function kept at cyclomatic complexity ~1 and only a line or two edited \u2014 the duplicate-detection logic itself lives entirely in the new low-complexity class.\n\nNote: the current `Owner` model has no soft-delete flag, so all persisted owners are considered; the normalization (digits-only) handles differently-formatted numbers that represent the same telephone.",
